---
title: skyBlip Go
nav_title: skyBlip Go
description: The pocket tracker, screen by screen · traffic drawn the way you see it, an alarm that gives you the angle, the four pages, the two contacts, and what the device does on the apron.
---

<section id="simulator">
  <p class="kicker">skyBlip Go</p>
  <h1>Switch one on. It is a real one&rsquo;s firmware running.</h1>

  <%= render "shared/simulator",
        wake: "Hold the lower key to switch it back on.",
        traffic: "Put an aircraft in the sky",
        keys: "Once it is on, the keyboard flies it while the pad has focus, and T puts another aircraft in the sky.",
        on: "running",
        off: "off",
        menu: "menu",
        glass: "The simulated e-paper panel of a skyBlip Go",
        key: "The device button: press to open the menu of the page you are on, hold two seconds to switch off, hold it again to switch on",
        pad: "The capacitive pad: tap to change page, hold one second to come back to the radar",
        reset: "RST: reboot the device",
        caption: "Sensors are simulated, the firmware is not. It is the build this site was published from.",
        missing: "The simulator is not part of this build of the site." %>

  <p class="note">
    The sky is empty until you ask for something. Every aircraft you add
    transmits real ADS-L frames, which the firmware receives, decodes and plots
    exactly as it would in flight. The lamp on the left is the firmware&rsquo;s:
    it lights when a contact is worth an alarm. The one on the right belongs to
    the charger, so it stays dark here. Every capture on these pages comes off this same
    firmware.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="kicker">Page by page</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    The rest of the device, one subject to a page.
    <%= link_to_page "features", label: "Every feature" %> is the list, one line
    each, and <%= link_to_page "displays", label: "every screen" %> is the
    picture, as the firmware draws it.
  </p>

  <div class="cards">
    <article class="card card--screen">
      <%= screen_image_tag "far-all.png", alt: "The radar page with PLOT ALL, traffic inside the ring and on the band around it" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "radar" %></h3>
      <p>Heading up, a minute of track ahead of each aircraft, an alarm that says where to look, and every aircraft heard on the glass.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card card--screen">
      <%= screen_image_tag "sixpack.png", alt: "The six-pack page" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "instruments" %></h3>
      <p>Six dials off the GNSS with the cell over the middle one, and a g-meter that keeps this flight's peaks.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card card--screen">
      <%= screen_image_tag "menu-radar.png", alt: "The settings menu" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "controls" %></h3>
      <p>Two contacts, the settings under the radar, a callsign typed on the device, and the diagnostic pages by name.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card card--screen">
      <%= screen_image_tag "off-flat-battery.png", alt: "The glass of a device that switched itself off on an empty cell" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "power" %></h3>
      <p>What it waits for on the apron, what off looks like, and a cell that says so when it runs out.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card card--screen">
      <%= screen_image_tag "confirm.png", alt: "The authorisation prompt on the glass" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "phone" %></h3>
      <p>Three apps at once with no pairing, every write asked on the glass, and firmware from a web page.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card card--screen">
      <%= screen_image_tag "radio-log.png", alt: "The radio log" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "radio" %></h3>
      <p>One radio, four dwells a second, and two systems heard in one of them.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card card--screen">
      <%= screen_image_tag "astern-all.png", alt: "The radar page with PLOT ALL and a group of aircraft astern" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "displays" %></h3>
      <p>Every screen in one place, and the radar drawn both ways.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card card--screen">
      <%= screen_image_tag "alarm.png", alt: "The radar page during a traffic advisory" %>
      <h3><%= link_to_page "features" %></h3>
      <p>Everything the device does, one line each, and where each one is explained.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <p>
    <%= link_to_page "devices", class: "cta" %>
    &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;
